{title: A Time for Everything}
{subtitle: Ecclesiastes 3:1–8}
{key: F}
{tempo: 97}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Chorus (instrumental)}
| [F] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] | ×2
| [F] | [Dm] |

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For [Bb]everything there is a season
[F]A time for every matter under heaven
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A [Dm]time to be born and a time to die
[Bb]A time to plant and [F]a time to uproot what is planted
[Dm]A time to kill and a [Bb]time to heal
A [F]time to tear down and a time [Dm]to build
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A [Dm]time to weep and a time to laugh
A [Bb]time to mourn and a time to dance
[F]A time to scatter stones and [Dm]a time to gather them
A time to em[Bb]brace and a time to [F]refrain from embracing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For [Dm]everything [Bb]there is a season
A time for ev[F]ery matter under heaven
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
A time to seek and [Dm]a time to lose
A time to keep and a [Bb]time to [F]throw away
A time to tear and a [Dm]time to mend
A time to be [Bb]silent and a time to speak
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
A time to love and a time to hate
A time for war and a time [F]for peace
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For everything there [Dm]is a sea[Bb]son
A time for every matter un[F]der heaven
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]A time for every matter under [F]heaven
{end_of_verse}
